# Documentation Maintenance for CLI Changes

This rule ensures that user-facing documentation stays in sync with the code.

## When Modifying CLI Commands

When adding, removing, or changing Click commands, subcommands, options, or
arguments in `src/tak/cli/main.py`, you **must** also update:

1. **README.md** -- the CLI Reference tables (grouped by Agent lifecycle,
   Interaction, Discovery and routing, Standalone).
2. **Click help strings** -- the `help=` parameter on each `@click.command()`,
   `@click.option()`, and `@click.argument()` decorator.
3. **Any docs/ files** that reference the changed command (e.g.
   `docs/tryout-guide.md`, `docs/PROJECT-STATUS.md`).

A change that alters the user-facing CLI surface without updating documentation
is incomplete.

## When Adding IPC Handlers

When adding a new handler in `src/tak/ipc/server.py` that exposes new
CLI-accessible functionality, update the README CLI Reference and any relevant
docs/ files.

## When Changing Configuration

When adding or modifying keys in `config/default.yaml` or `config/agents.yaml`,
update `AGENTS.md` and any docs/ files that describe configuration options.
